Sat Oct 24 10:50:10 UTC 2026 - Eyad Issa <eyadlorenzo@gmail.com>

- Refresh disable-tidy-tests.patch for the 0.11.0 source layout
- Require Rust 1.99.0 or newer to build Wild
- Update to version 0.11.0:
  * Enable the Wasm feature by default. Wild can now link Wasm
    modules, though debug information is not supported yet.
  * Greatly expand GNU linker script support. Wild can now link
    Linux kernel modules and is close to linking the Linux kernel.
  * Advance the Mac port: Wild can link itself on Mac, and a
    maintainer now uses it as the default linker for Rust on Mac.
    The port is not enabled by default yet.
  * Improve performance on several filesystems and add general
    optimizations. ELF COMDAT support adds some overhead.
  * Limit default threads to 32 to avoid contention on Linux's
    per-inode mutex; --threads can override the limit.
  * Expand benchmarks to cover more filesystems and existing or new
    output files.
  * Add linker script commands and expressions, section attributes,
    symbol and alignment handling, orphan handling, and additional
    GNU linker options. Add AArch64, x86_64, and ppc64le
    relocation and relaxation support.
  * Add --image-base, --only-keep-debug, --no-keep-memory,
    --discard-*, executable stack, and linker version options.
  * Improve parallel archive parsing, partial linking, relocation
    processing, debug relocation handling, memory allocation, and
    filesystem output handling.
  * Fix linker script symbols and location counters, LTO and
    dynamic symbols, TLS and PLT relocations, GOT/PLT relaxation,
    ELF properties and section handling, archive/shared-library
    selection, and deterministic output.
  * Extend Wasm linking with shared-memory TLS, exports, stripping,
    feature checks, section retention, and symbol handling.
  * Advance Mach-O linking with dylib, TLS, fixup, exports, and
    compact unwind support. Add COFF link.exe-style argument
    parsing.
  * See the full changelog at
    /usr/share/doc/packages/wild/CHANGELOG.md.

